ct's ruins","description":"Tolland Station becomes the Hulk; the Key of Office becomes a trophy; the Roll's last pages become the Kin's prayer book.","createdAt":1792004966388,"updatedAt":1792004966388,"version":1},{"id":"IJNza0vGnqOw_JLB0M_ko","worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","sourceTimelineId":"XiOosvS4HJ4RDWPn0l1G-","targetTimelineId":"2C_KFJInWvb7XqYycox3b","type":"historical_echo","anchors":[],"syncPoints":[],"label":"The Compact tells the Mercy's story wrongly","description":"Same hull, same key, same book of names. The Compact's founding myth (the Breach, the Opener) is the Mercy's last weeks told by the man who won.","createdAt":1792004961657,"updatedAt":1792004961657,"version":1}],"crossTimelineArtifacts":[{"id":"64TdEjXrJAdF6p3PkyTAQ","worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","itemId":"Q_DoL-UpW5ZUBmO9bwT-v","originTimelineId":"2C_KFJInWvb7XqYycox3b","encounterTimelineId":"cWTtwvDU23FxyxXommY3Q","encounterNotes":"hanging on an iron peg behind Marrow Fane's desk","createdAt":1792005147930,"updatedAt":1792005147930,"version":1},{"id":"7DjOQiY4e1kROsYI3ut9T","worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","itemId":"bu1kJTRuR9m937p4WCaCe","originTimelineId":"2C_KFJInWvb7XqYycox3b","encounterTimelineId":"cWTtwvDU23FxyxXommY3Q","encounterNotes":"Rows 28\u201334, sewn into red Union cloth: Kit's prayer book","createdAt":1792005155000,"updatedAt":1792005155000,"version":1},{"id":"LskZgP-3ZKuqPHFiYKl04","worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","itemId":"bI9Y1FNY21qm9DDy_Lcw6","originTimelineId":"2C_KFJInWvb7XqYycox3b","encounterTimelineId":"cWTtwvDU23FxyxXommY3Q","encounterNotes":"in the wreck of the Obedient, deep in the Grind","createdAt":1792005162064,"updatedAt":1792005162064,"version":1},{"id":"Y4ToPwLgi0OfsGXhtNmmP","worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","itemId":"YwiMeYg1lXIoDRGJykqE7","originTimelineId":"XiOosvS4HJ4RDWPn0l1G-","encounterTimelineId":"2C_KFJInWvb7XqYycox3b","encounterNotes":"under glass in the Hall of Muster, scorched and missing a brass corner","createdAt":1792005133800,"updatedAt":1792005133800,"version":1},{"id":"Y_NdDodDrRJao3iofBoxW","worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","itemId":"Q_DoL-UpW5ZUBmO9bwT-v","originTimelineId":"XiOosvS4HJ4RDWPn0l1G-","encounterTimelineId":"2C_KFJInWvb7XqYycox3b","encounterNotes":"worn on a chain as the Key of Office by every Warden-General","createdAt":1792005140865,"updatedAt":1792005140865,"version":1}],"mapRoutes":[],"mapRegions":[{"id":"Xsef3Zi-nNg3H0i1OyRRT","linkedMapLayerId":null,"factionId":null,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","mapLayerId":"_He5HO1KES1AkTNXs_Zls","name":"Interdict Field","vertices":[{"x":983.8331160365059,"y":755.671447196871},{"x":1381.7470664928294,"y":795.8279009126468},{"x":1454.7588005215125,"y":449.0221642764016},{"x":1100.651890482399,"y":397.9139504563234}],"fillColor":"#60a5fa","opacity":0.35,"createdAt":1791999309683,"updatedAt":1791999309683,"version":1}],"mapRegionSnapshots":[],"mapAnnotations":[],"loreCategories":[{"id":"85eaQj37TogiZA_DWoxwC","sortOrder":2,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","name":"Folklore & Faith","color":"#6366f1"},{"id":"gocUlEnETBYv_X9jT2yME","sortOrder":0,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","name":"History","color":"#6366f1"},{"id":"jocasQBeUI6AxdDX-h80A","sortOrder":1,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","name":"Law & Charter","color":"#6366f1"},{"id":"kxco_NPJ-TkZ8pqCOLKwN","sortOrder":3,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","name":"Ships & Machines","color":"#6366f1"}],"lorePages":[{"id":"8obCh8-3-oaBj85eY3kNz","body":"The sleeper hold of the *Mercy of Tolland*: a great flat drum across the ship's spine, forty rows of berths spoked out from a central gangway, a hundred to a row.\n\nEvery berth carries a plate \u2014 name, age, trade, a four-figure number (row and berth: *3112* is Row Thirty-One, berth twelve) \u2014 and a *dream index* light that, as every warden eventually discovers, is wired to nothing.\n\nThe hold is kept by its **warden-engineer**, who holds the only manual key to its lock-bolts and is expected to listen to the compressors the way a nurse listens to a chest. Twelve wardens in a hundred and ninety years; their initials are scratched round the key's collar.\n\n> The cold rows did not sing. People who had never worked Deck Nine said they did.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["mGxbTHrLW4jI6oKhIx_7e","LXUXgA4wS1ieLl7SGh-py","Q_DoL-UpW5ZUBmO9bwT-v"],"visibleFromEventId":"aFQn-cBt6tiKf-YEEJJFS","createdAt":1792003973159,"updatedAt":1792003981249,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","categoryId":"kxco_NPJ-TkZ8pqCOLKwN","title":"Deck Nine","version":5},{"id":"DEO9toWXySi2A-vifPURc","body":"The song of the Ninefold Kin. The first forty families on the ice, in the forties AL, heard it through the ice east of where Calloway's Rift runs dry: a low continuous hum, *like a great many voices a very long way off, all holding the same note.*\n\nThe Navy moved them back. The Kin did what they were told, and made a song:\n\n> There's a choir in the ice and it never stops,\n> it's been singing since the long night drops,\n> and the Warden's eye says go no nearer,\n> but the song gets clearer and the song gets clearer \u2014\n> so we keep the count, we keep the count,\n> till the long night's over.\n\nLater versions, sung as lullabies in Gallows Town, carry a map in them: *forty from the Gallows where the Rift runs dry.*","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["k6mwWYvDFgoZfnd4D7B5m","rebp6zTC03AHNl06A4zti","GAVYuM30sRMr0QyVo1MsA"],"visibleFromEventId":"-xco6-C-HrTUTl2ffNwzy","createdAt":1792004017626,"updatedAt":1792004025762,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","categoryId":"85eaQj37TogiZA_DWoxwC","title":"The Cold Choir","version":5},{"id":"KHe00UOeGQCKode6Hczxu","body":"**Order the First of the Wardenry**, year One after Landfall: an area of the surface of Ninefold within forty kilometres of a stated point is closed to all persons in perpetuity \u2014 no landing, drilling, survey or dwelling, on pain of death. Signed only *Warden*, at the instruction of the Captain, and sealed with the shape of a key.\n\nUpheld by every Warden-General for three hundred years and enforced by a Navy cutter on station above the point. Never explained.\n\nThe Gallows survey of 309 AL found the ice under the Field clean to a thousand metres \u2014 the richest water in the Reach. The Ninefold Ice Union asked for it at the talks of 310. The Warden-General said *no*.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["k6mwWYvDFgoZfnd4D7B5m","7ZNq1_qn7gwW7-y6J3aZ2","fKieCBsNE-j7KAAlSK-Ct"],"visibleFromEventId":"A-FY7Nsk-WNvo5oEcOFBQ","createdAt":1792003995375,"updatedAt":1792004003475,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","categoryId":"jocasQBeUI6AxdDX-h80A","title":"The Interdict Field","version":5},{"id":"RtSQMqpgKhvEAHMl-vLoK","body":"The founding instrument of the Colony of Tolland, forty pages on cream paper, sealed in red wax in a Company strongbox in the quartermaster's store: *not to be opened before Landfall except by order of the Master*.\n\n**Article the First.** The colony, the ship and everything in the destination system are held in common by the **Members** \u2014 the persons embarked in cold passage according to the Muster.\n\n**Article the Second.** The officers and crew and their issue born in passage are **bonded servants** of the Colony until ten years after Landfall.\n\n**Article the Ninth.** Should the Members be *lost entire*, title passes to the surviving complement of the vessel, released forthwith from bond.\n\nEvery officer of the *Mercy* sat the Company examination on it. Burned in the fire in the stores, 1 BL.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["7Qd3d0Xlv0W1nhsd_Iyra","XiG3_An1XCamJg4EQPbxG"],"visibleFromEventId":"KrbFznN4lQevhKrzHtvZW","createdAt":1792004006744,"updatedAt":1792004014359,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","categoryId":"jocasQBeUI6AxdDX-h80A","title":"The Tolland Charter","version":5},{"id":"TTTSt5mjRZdJiVI-3GDzt","body":"The long fall of the Compact through the fourth and fifth centuries after Landfall.\n\nIt began, the Kin say, on the Tricentennial of 311 AL, when the First Warden's words went up on every screen of the Spine and a crowd broke open the Watch-house; the Wardenry outlived that day by a century and a half, but never again ruled by consent. Ninefold's ice works ran down, the Navy's cutters were lost one by one in the Scree, the Kesh Faith dwindled to a chapel, and Tolland Station became *the Hulk*.\n\nBy 742 AL the Reach has no government, one money-lender, and a great many wrecks.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["zcFaDeue-UWwkd5SwOmmb","4jf9axgqen2qDyUdWny3I"],"visibleFromEventId":"gbxCLZ1yxrqRtb6fFWRlZ","createdAt":1792004050757,"updatedAt":1792004058356,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","categoryId":"gocUlEnETBYv_X9jT2yME","title":"The Unraveling","version":5},{"id":"Y1h3nP1IUNpp4YJVYn_j2","body":"A generation hauler of the Tolland Colonial Company, launched from Earth orbit and a hundred and ninety years in passage to the red dwarf Cauld.\n\n**Length** 1.1 km along the Spine. **Waking crew** 340, in two spun rings. **Sleepers** 4,000, in the cold rows of Deck Nine.\n\n## Lives of the hull\n\n- **1 BL** \u2014 a ship, decelerating into the Reach for two months on its great engines, the spin stopped and *down* become *aft*.\n- **11 AL onward** \u2014 the core of *Tolland Station*, capital of the Compact. The Spine becomes a street; the bridge becomes the Warden-General's residence; the forward hold becomes the Hall of Muster.\n- **742 AL** \u2014 *the Hulk*. Lights going out section by section, a few thousand scavengers living in the warm part round the docks, and Marrow Fane's Counting House in the bow, where the light is best.\n\nThe captain's brass bell hangs on the bridge in all three. It is rung for a launch, a landfall, and the death of a captain.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["zcFaDeue-UWwkd5SwOmmb","mGxbTHrLW4jI6oKhIx_7e","X-RTBLHErhKR9ZtgUT5E5","4jf9axgqen2qDyUdWny3I"],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1792003888532,"updatedAt":1792003962889,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","categoryId":"kxco_NPJ-TkZ8pqCOLKwN","title":"The Mercy of Tolland","version":4},{"id":"aYWKkLBKlrf8H2mI_wPev","body":"*SLEEPER HOLD (DECK NINE). SEPARABLE CONFIGURATION.* Found in a waterproof sleeve in the pilot cell under the drum, where nobody had been since the yard.\n\nThe hold was built as a **contingency lander**: eight retro-packs in the Drop Bay gallery, an ablative keel under its floor, a pilot cell for *manual descent only, one crew*, and a sealed standby core under Row Twenty *rated for one thousand years at standby load \u2014 sufficient to maintain the hold indefinitely on the surface of a cold body, pending recovery.*\n\nThe Company's accountants took it out of the manuals.\n\nRevised in grease pencil under the title block: **REV. I. VARGA \u2014 9 YIELD. DESCENT TO NINEFOLD FEASIBLE. MARGINS POOR. PILOT CELL NOT RATED FOR SURFACE IMPACT.**","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["mGxbTHrLW4jI6oKhIx_7e","LXUXgA4wS1ieLl7SGh-py"],"visibleFromEventId":"lkMCWlFXKn8YDaCFpQOoX","createdAt":1792004039875,"updatedAt":1792004047490,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","categoryId":"kxco_NPJ-TkZ8pqCOLKwN","title":"Yard Drawing 7/C","version":5},{"id":"bC53aGZzIMgsU7gfT9kgG","body":"*The account taught in every schoolroom of the Compact.*\n\nOn the Fifth Quiet Day of 1 BL, at the start of the Landfall burn, the release stations of the sleeper hold were opened by hand **without authority and against the Captain's order**. The hold separated from the ship under thrust and was lost, together with all four thousand Members of the Colony asleep in it.\n\nThe act was that of one person, *the Opener*, warden-engineer of the hold, whose name was cut out of the record by the Father's order and is not to be spoken in the Hall of Muster. The Opener did not survive.\n\nThe surviving crew bound themselves into the Compact by the **Charter of Survivors**, signed on Landfall Day, 11 AL.\n\n*Those who were not woken* are honoured on every Landfall Day.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["mGxbTHrLW4jI6oKhIx_7e","YwiMeYg1lXIoDRGJykqE7"],"visibleFromEventId":"_L6l3j8WW4mAwtZ0Wjj16","createdAt":1792003984508,"updatedAt":1792003992114,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","categoryId":"gocUlEnETBYv_X9jT2yME","title":"The Breach at Landfall","version":5},{"id":"fgLf5q-nyFxxi0nLztml4","body":"The central text of the Kesh Faith, chanted every Landfall Day.\n\n> And the Father brought them across the dark,\n> out of the old world into the new.\n> And at the Landfall there was a breach,\n> and the Opener opened the locks of the Ninth Deck\n> and gave the Four Thousand to the dark.\n> And the Father wept, and took the Key from the Opener's hand,\n> and put it on his own breast,\n> that his children should never forget to watch.\n\nThe Faith burned one heresy above all others, and the man who wrote it. It was five words long: *the Opener was the only one who kept faith.*","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["Q_DoL-UpW5ZUBmO9bwT-v","3UHWEEdv1Nz8fLrFRstqt"],"visibleFromEventId":"54os9ueXEVay1bGczw7FV","createdAt":1792004029043,"updatedAt":1792004036611,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","categoryId":"85eaQj37TogiZA_DWoxwC","title":"The Litany of the Crossing","version":5},{"id":"gSPbM2qbFNI7Uqug3H-G3","body":"The calendar of the Cauld Reach, counted from **Landfall**.\n\nTwelve months of thirty days \u2014 *Firstwatch, Ember, Haul, Thaw, Lode, Brine, Midhold, Rust, Ballast, Ashfall, Longdark, Yield* \u2014 and the five **Quiet Days** outside them at the year's end, which the ship kept as rest days and the Compact as days of mourning.\n\nYears before Landfall count down as **BL**; the Mercy's last year in passage is *1 BL*. Landfall itself is the first day of *1 AL*. Every Landfall Day the Compact read the first and last names of the Four Thousand aloud in the Hall of Muster.\n\n- *The Mercy*: Longdark \u2013 the Fifth Quiet Day, 1 BL.\n- *The Compact*: Yield 310 \u2013 1 Firstwatch 311 AL (the Tricentennial of the Charter of Survivors).\n- *The Quiet*: Rust 742 AL.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1792003966163,"updatedAt":1792003970104,"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","categoryId":"gocUlEnETBYv_X9jT2yME","title":"The Reach Reckoning","version":3}],"factions":[{"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","name":"The Kesh Faith","description":"The religion of the Father: Aurel Kesh as saint, the Opener as devil, the Key as relic. By 742 AL one drunk priest and eleven candles.","color":"#ec4899","coverImageId":null,"tags":[],"id":"-YMFh5dvmuv0PN1JXotb6","createdAt":1792003557614,"updatedAt":1792003741098,"version":2},{"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","name":"The Counting House","description":"Marrow Fane's money-lending house on the Hulk, 742 AL. Owns everybody's paper.","color":"#8b5cf6","coverImageId":null,"tags":[],"id":"C2M3N_BmS6nolCQKmaADF","createdAt":1792003555999,"updatedAt":1792003737663,"version":2},{"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","name":"Ninefold Ice Union","description":"The miners of the Gallows quadrant, red hand on the shoulder. On strike since Longdark 310 after the Shaft Twelve collapse.","color":"#14b8a6","coverImageId":null,"tags":[],"id":"Hc46yZeGDYbnqjLrhZVf3","createdAt":1792003552749,"updatedAt":1792003727123,"version":2},{"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","name":"Ship's Watch","description":"The Mercy's security watch: stun-batons and animal tranquilliser pistols, a corporal and a dozen hands. Keeps the hatches.","color":"#f97316","coverImageId":null,"tags":[],"id":"ZYnDRwyjYsPp8qhNfNOMW","createdAt":1792003547933,"updatedAt":1792003715002,"version":2},{"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","name":"The Mercy's Crew","description":"The three hundred and forty waking crew of the generation hauler Mercy of Tolland, 1 BL: bonded servants of the Colony under the Tolland Charter, born aboard and dying aboard for six generations.","color":"#ef4444","coverImageId":null,"tags":[],"id":"ZagBL1FqMOiqgMz4ZfNlm","createdAt":1792003493635,"updatedAt":1792003700612,"version":2},{"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","name":"Compact Navy","description":"The Compact's fleet of cutters. The Obedient kept station over the Interdict Field every day for decades.","color":"#22c55e","coverImageId":null,"tags":[],"id":"fqNgVfAA2WDD999hLmoFe","createdAt":1792003551159,"updatedAt":1792003723677,"version":2},{"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","name":"The Ninefold Kin","description":"The descendants of the forty first families on the ice. They paint their walls with names, sing the song of the choir in the ice, and keep the count.","color":"#3b82f6","coverImageId":null,"tags":[],"id":"kUzNr6RliMSAfMBI3MFSj","createdAt":1792003554372,"updatedAt":1792003730586,"version":2},{"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","name":"The Compact","description":"The government of the Cauld Reach from 11 AL: the Charter of Survivors, the hereditary Wardenry of the Kesh line, the Hall of Muster. Rules from Tolland Station. Begins to unravel after the Tricentennial of 311 AL.","color":"#eab308","coverImageId":null,"tags":[],"id":"sAUgUrpz6L_cCetDbcsCn","createdAt":1792003549533,"updatedAt":1792003718442,"version":2}],"factionMemberships":[{"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","factionId":"-YMFh5dvmuv0PN1JXotb6","characterId":"Er9sM6SWRQkV5X6lhRZm5","role":null,"startEventId":null,"endEventId":null,"notes":"","id":"6LBssB6WFWlIlb72v7B4F","createdAt":1792003742518,"updatedAt":1792003742518,"version":1},{"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","factionId":"kUzNr6RliMSAfMBI3MFSj","characterId":"WIHijinlYh_XtLLwh55Wj","role":null,"startEventId":null,"endEventId":null,"notes":"","id":"8V7OmLFGH14hOX2gRJdGt","createdAt":1792003732001,"updatedAt":1792003732001,"version":1},{"worldId":"WrAObMdV1iWydr79-9UFa","factionId":"ZagBL1FqMOiqgMz4ZfNlm","characterId":"rF9q0I-cFStCoUa92LlLq","role":null,"startEventId":null,"endEventId":null,"notes":"","id":"CoCT6LIZUbx1LbIfGtsju","createdAt":179200